For a Java team, a controlled evaluation might include explaining an unfamiliar service, proposing tests for a failure path and drafting an API migration note. Each output should be checked against the repository rather than accepted because it sounds plausible. The model is one component of a production system; authentication, access controls and observability remain the application''s responsibility.

The interesting question is not whether a new model feels more intelligent. It is whether it helps a specific team produce correct work with less review effort and predictable cost.','OpenAI','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-02 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

An engineer investigating a failing servlet filter can ask for a hypothesis, but the strongest process still starts with a reproducible test. The assistant should identify assumptions, explain why a proposed change is limited in scope and show how to detect a regression. Long explanations are not evidence by themselves.

Comparisons should use consistent tasks, repository snapshots and time budgets. Otherwise the result measures prompt-writing luck as much as model quality.','OpenAI','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-03 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

A robust integration keeps the provider call behind a typed interface. Requests have bounded sizes, deadlines and validated parameters. Outputs are parsed into application DTOs and rejected when required fields are missing. Logs record latency and error categories without exposing private input data.

Begin with a narrow use case such as classifying internal documentation. Once reliability is understood, expand to more complex workflows with clear human approval points.','OpenAI','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-04 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

This changes the job of the application around the model. Tool calls must be authorized and logged, risky actions should be reversible, and an agent needs explicit stopping conditions. A successful demonstration in a clean sample repository is not the same as safe operation inside a production codebase.

For development teams, a useful pilot gives the agent one contained feature and asks a separate reviewer to verify tests and behavior. The quality of that handoff matters as much as the model itself.','Anthropic','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-05 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Documentation cleanup, straightforward test generation and well-scoped UI adjustments are candidates for lighter model usage. Architecture changes, security-sensitive logic and ambiguous incidents may justify more time and capacity. Neither category should be decided from model branding alone.

A team can route requests by complexity while measuring failed attempts, reviewer corrections and total cost per accepted change. The cheapest individual request is not necessarily the cheapest finished feature.','Anthropic','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-06 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Instead of arguing about which model is universally better, maintain a small evaluation suite drawn from completed issues. Include a simple bug, a cross-file refactor and a case where a seemingly reasonable suggestion would violate an existing project convention. Ask reviewers to grade actual diffs rather than explanations.

The result may be a mixed workflow: one model for planning, another for implementation and a deterministic test suite that has the final word.','Anthropic','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-07 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Consider a web application that has to understand a bug report containing text, an image and snippets of source code. The developer should examine which inputs the model accepts, how the API expresses them and how errors appear in the response. A screenshot can provide context, but it may also contain tokens, customer data or internal URLs.

The safest way to evaluate a new model is with representative, sanitized tasks and published acceptance criteria. Product announcements are a starting point, not a migration plan.','Google','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-08 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

For a multi-module CMS, an agent might inspect route definitions, implement a service method and update a frontend client. The most important orchestration feature may be the ability to show the proposed files and ask for confirmation before a database migration or security change.

A model''s strength should be judged through complete, reviewable change sets. When the task crosses multiple boundaries, a locked API contract prevents individually convincing components from disagreeing.','Google','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-09 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Reading repository files is different from committing a change; drafting a migration is different from applying it. Those actions should be represented explicitly in tool policies. An assistant that can execute tests offers a stronger feedback loop than one that only produces code snippets, yet it still needs guardrails around destructive commands.

Teams comparing coding assistants should record tool access, prompt constraints and verification steps alongside model results. Without that context, demonstrations are difficult to reproduce.','Google','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-10 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

That convenience comes with a risk: visual context is easy to overinterpret. A screenshot may reveal the symptom but not the root cause. The assistant should use the image to form hypotheses, then request the relevant code path or a reproducible test. Teams also need a habit of removing personal information before sharing captures.

The most useful outcome is a more complete problem description, not an unverified fix assembled from a picture.','Google','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-11 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

A team considering local inference should test the entire path: model distribution, hardware requirements, serving software, monitoring and updates. The cost of operating GPUs and handling incidents can exceed the savings suggested by a per-token comparison.

