Self-hosting adds responsibilities that a prototype may hide: capacity planning, model loading time, request queues, security patches and fallback behavior when a server fails. A managed endpoint still demands vendor risk assessment, rate-limit handling and strict control over what information is transmitted.

A realistic comparison uses expected traffic, peak concurrency and a defined service-level target. Choosing a hosting model is an operational decision as much as an AI decision.','DeepSeek','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-10-13 00:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

A clean architecture hides provider-specific request details behind an adapter while preserving meaningful capabilities such as structured output and tool calls. The temptation to create a universal interface for every possible model feature should be resisted; a small, typed contract is easier to test.

