Include endpoint paths, DTO fields, validation rules, transaction behavior and failure responses. Spell out whether an absent dependency should be implemented or whether work is explicitly out of scope. Acceptance criteria should be observable: a test passes, a route returns expected JSON or a migration runs safely.

The best prompt reduces decisions that would otherwise be deferred to another agent. It leaves implementation freedom without leaving contracts ambiguous.','WORKFLOW','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-09 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Before writing code, the agent should inspect how servlets are registered, where security checks happen and how DAO methods obtain connections. A new feature should follow those patterns instead of introducing a second dependency-injection framework or a competing error handler.

A stable architecture benefits from consistency more than novelty. AI assistance is valuable when it makes careful additions to the system that exists.','JAVA','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-10 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Read the migration as a production change. Ask what happens when the table is not empty, whether identifiers are reused and how the application behaves during deployment. For PostgreSQL, test the migration against a representative database snapshot, then inspect indexes and constraints.

