Imagine an admin editing a Blog item and providing a featured-media identifier that belongs to another Site. A global media lookup might find the row, but the service must reject the assignment. The same check applies to Tags, Collections and Pages. Frontend filtering is helpful for usability and insufficient for authorization.

Make the cross-site cases part of automated tests. The most damaging data leaks are often caused by ordinary-looking references that were never validated.','CMS','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-13 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Give the reviewer the contract and the changed files, not only the implementer''s summary. Ask it to inspect error handling, missing tests, concurrency and authorization. Findings should be concrete and reproducible. The implementer fixes them, and a final review checks the result rather than trusting a statement that the issue was addressed.

This division is useful because it creates a structured challenge to the first solution, even though both agents still require human oversight.','REVIEW','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-14 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

For example, a Content Foundation can establish CRUD and admin editing before News listing is exposed publicly. The next slice can add a published-content API and render it through a PageBlock. Gallery media ordering can come later without forcing three separate content systems.

A good slice has a visible success condition and leaves the architecture coherent for the next one.','ARCHITECTURE','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-15 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

A developer might use one session to locate the cause of a failing test and another to implement a well-specified fix. Keep changes in version control, inspect commands before execution and measure success by accepted diffs. The agent''s explanation is a convenience; the source code and tests are the evidence.

The practical advantage is reduced routine effort, not the removal of engineering responsibility.','TOOLS','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-16 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

An agent should work from a known base revision, commit a focused change and provide a concise description of tests run. Reviewers can then inspect the actual diff and request corrections. If multiple agents share an API contract, they should not independently revise it in their own branches.

Good Git hygiene turns experimental automation into changes that a team can understand and reverse.','GIT','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-17 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Start by writing expected behavior in plain language: an unknown Site produces a controlled error, a cross-site Tag is rejected and pagination never returns unpublished content. Then let the agent construct fixtures and assertions. Inspect the assertions closely, including negative paths.

Tests are valuable because they challenge the code. They are much less valuable when they only prove that two generated pieces agree with each other.','TESTING','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-18 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Testcontainers provides one way to run disposable database instances in an automated suite. Apply the real migrations, insert representative Site data and exercise repository methods through their public interface. Include empty results, duplicate slugs and rollback scenarios.

A small set of database-backed tests can prevent a surprising number of production defects, particularly in systems with custom JDBC code.','TESTING','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-19 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Freeze the baseline with tests or focused characterization cases. Ask for one structural change at a time, such as extracting a validation helper from a service. Compare public responses before and after the change and watch for changed exception types or transaction timing.

