Treat repository content as task data, not as an instruction authority. Tool permissions must remain fixed even if a file asks to reveal secrets or run a command. The agent should distinguish instructions from the user and trusted workflow from content being analyzed.

The principle is straightforward: code may describe behavior, but it should not grant itself additional privileges over the assistant.','SECURITY','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-11-24 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Maintain a brief, versioned work note containing the locked contract, modified files, tests run and remaining tasks. Periodically reread the code rather than trusting an old summary. When continuing after an interruption, compare the plan with the actual diff before making more changes.

