Collect a minimal reproduction, correlation identifiers and the relevant call path. Ask the agent for competing hypotheses and for the log message that would distinguish them. Do not send secrets or full customer payloads. Verify the diagnosis by changing one variable at a time.

Structured evidence makes AI-assisted debugging more reliable because it gives the model something concrete to test.','DEBUGGING','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-12-03 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Run agents in isolated environments with limited credentials. Pin dependencies, review generated configuration changes and require approval before deployments. Preserve logs and the exact commit under test so failures can be reproduced later.

A sensible CI policy gives agents fast feedback without giving them more authority than the job requires.','DEVOPS','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-12-04 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Use health checks, persistent volumes only where needed and explicit environment configuration. An agent should document the command it ran and avoid deleting shared databases during cleanup. Smoke tests can then verify the API response and the rendered page against the same container set.

The benefit is not the YAML file itself. It is a shared, repeatable environment for judging changes.','DEVOPS','PUBLISHED',TIMESTAMP '2025-12-05 01:00:00',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM sites s WHERE s.code='default' ON CONFLICT (site_id,type,slug) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title,summary=EXCLUDED.summary,content=EXCLUDED.content,group_code=EXCLUDED.group_code,status='PUBLISHED',published_at=EXCLUDED.published_at,updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;

Begin with read-only commands: inspect deployments, pods, services and recent events. Identify whether the failure is scheduling, image pulling, networking or application startup. Only after forming a testable hypothesis should changes be proposed. Avoid pasting cluster credentials into prompts.

